/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 76 0 R
/T (    This weekend \(November 14th/15th\), the Church celebrates the Thirty-third Sunday in Ordinary Time. Entering the last two weeks of our liturgical year, our readings have a certain sense of finality to them. Yet, this finality is not meant to be seen as an ending, but a new beginning. Just as the old year gives way to the new, so the Christian life is always pushing us towards that movement from the old man to the new: From death to life.)
/E (    This weekend \(November 14th/15th\), the Church celebrates the Thirty-third Sunday in Ordinary Time. Entering the last two weeks of our liturgical year, our readings have a certain sense of finality to them. Yet, this finality is not meant to be seen as an ending, but a new beginning. Just as the old year gives way to the new, so the Christian life is always pushing us towards that movement from the old man to the new: From death to life.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4 7 5 8 6 9]
>>
